# APT source for the official Proxmox VE repository, deb822 format.
#
# One file, both architectures.  The repository publishes binary-amd64 and
# binary-arm64 under the same suite and component, so nothing here branches on
# the target architecture.  Confirmed against the live InRelease, which declares
# `Architectures: amd64 arm64`.
#
# pve-no-subscription rather than pve-enterprise: the enterprise component
# requires a subscription key that a published image cannot carry.  The two
# components track the same versions; enterprise lags by a validation cycle.
#
# The keyring this refers to is fetched and checksum-verified in the
# Containerfile.  Signed-By is a path rather than an inline key so the
# verification step and the trust decision stay in one place.
Types: deb
URIs: http://download.proxmox.com/debian/pve
Suites: trixie
Components: pve-no-subscription
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/proxmox-archive-keyring.gpg
